    "done_when": "Two defects that reviews of landed nodes found in the shared helpers' callers are repaired.\n\n1. reckon/_store.py:write_json_atomically. When the chmod that applies a requested mode raises, the empty sibling temporary it created stays on disk, although the module promises that a failure leaves neither a partial destination nor a stray sibling. Every failure after the temporary is created now removes it.\n2. reckon/crew/query.py:_normalize_stamp and reckon/crew/rollout.py:_parse_timestamp. Both test whether a stamp states its zone with a predicate that accepts only a trailing Z or z, or an offset ending in minutes. So 2026-09-29T01:02:03+00:00:30, an offset carrying seconds, is read as naming no zone. query returns (None, \"unknown\") and rollout returns a naive datetime, where base c786e44a returned (\"2026-09-29T01:01:33+00:00\", \"utc\") and an aware 2026-09-29T01:01:33+00:00. The zone test reads the parsed result's tzinfo rather than the text's shape, and both outputs match base.\n\ntests/test_shared_helper_edges.py covers both:\n- A chmod that raises, patched in, leaves no file in the directory other than the untouched destination.\n- The seconds-offset stamp gives the base outputs above for both callers.\nThe expectations are recorded at base cea6da07 by running the base code where they concern existing behaviour.\n\nThat file, tests/test_timestamp_callers_batch_a.py, tests/test_writer_callers_first_wave.py and tests/test_one_atomic_writer_and_number_decoder.py pass at exit 0. The manifest writes baseline_suite and after_suite each as one line of armed JSON: revision, command with no placeholder, exit_status, completed, failure_count, failure_ids, log_path. The head arm runs at the committed head. Every gate log opens with one line naming its revision, tree and command. The declared negative control is applied and observed to fail, and its log's absolute path is in the manifest with an EXIT= line and the FAILED id. The full project suite is not run by this node.",
    "estimated_hours": null,
    "goal": "Repair the two edge defects reviews found after the first migration wave: a failed chmod leaves the shared writer's temporary behind, and an offset carrying seconds reads as naming no zone in query and rollout",
